  "id": "COMPOUND:1716 - PROTEIN:1984",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Monoisopropylphosphorylserine and Tyrosine-protein phosphatase YopH, mediated through the ATP phosphoribosyltransferase enzyme. This is supported by three distinct pathways, each linking Monoisopropylphosphorylserine to the target enzyme via different intermediates. In all cases, Monoisopropylphosphorylserine is identified as a target of ATP phosphoribosyltransferase, which in turn is targeted by various compounds, including 3-Phenylpropylamine, Phosphorylisopropane, and Phenethylamine. These intermediates ultimately interact with Tyrosine-protein phosphatase YopH, indicating a possible regulatory or enzymatic pathway involving phosphoribosyltransferase. The scores from the three paths suggest a consistent pattern of interaction, though the strength of the evidence varies slightly. The mechanism appears to involve the phosphorylation of ATP phosphoribosyltransferase, which may influence the activity of Tyrosine-protein phosphatase YopH, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
